menu "Gravity cube"

config CUBE_LED_GPIO
    int "LED data GPIO"
    default 2
    help
        Data line of the WS2812 chain, through a 74AHCT125 level shifter
        and a 330 ohm series resistor. GPIO 2 is on the T-Display-S3's
        header and is not a strapping pin on the ESP32-S3.

config CUBE_FRAME_MS
    int "Physics step period (ms)"
    default 18
    range 5 100
    help
        One physics step per period. The physics constants are per step,
        so a longer period slows the fluid down. A fluid step takes about
        17 ms on the ESP32-S3, so 18 ms (55 steps a second) is the
        shortest period it keeps up with; the LED chain needs ~11.5 ms.

config CUBE_PANEL_TEST
    bool "Panel test at power on"
    default y
    help
        Before the fluid starts, fill each panel green LED by LED, from
        the bottom left row by row to the top right, in chain order (Left,
        Back, Right, Front, Bottom, Top): about 0.8 seconds a panel. A dead
        LED or panel, or a broken link in the chain, shows up straight
        away: every panel after a break stays dark.

config CUBE_TAP_THRESHOLD_MG
    int "Tap threshold (mg)"
    default 1000
    range 300 4000
    help
        Jump in acceleration between two samples (4 ms apart) that counts
        as a tap. Raise it if sloshing the fluid changes its colour, lower
        it if double taps are missed.

config CUBE_IMU_SPI_MOSI
    int "SPI MOSI GPIO (board SDA/SDI)"
    default 11

config CUBE_IMU_SPI_MISO
    int "SPI MISO GPIO (board AD0/SDO)"
    default 13

config CUBE_IMU_SPI_SCLK
    int "SPI SCLK GPIO (board SCL)"
    default 12

config CUBE_IMU_SPI_CS
    int "SPI CS GPIO (board NCS)"
    default 10

config CUBE_IMU_I2C_SCAN
    bool "Scan for I2C devices on the IMU pins at startup"
    default n
    help
        Wiring check: before setting up SPI, hold NCS high (which puts the
        MPU-6500 on I2C) and probe every address with SCL on the SCLK pin
        and SDA on the MOSI pin. An MPU-6500 answers at 0x68 (AD0 low) or
        0x69 (AD0 high). The SPI setup turns the chip's I2C interface off
        until it is power cycled, so the scan only finds it after a power
        on, not after a reset.

menu "Wi-Fi and firmware updates"

config CUBE_WIFI_SSID
    string "Wi-Fi SSID"
    default ""
    help
        Network to join for firmware updates over Wi-Fi. Empty turns Wi-Fi
        off, and with it updates over Wi-Fi.

config CUBE_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "Wi-Fi password"
    default ""
    help
        Empty for an open network.

config CUBE_HOSTNAME
    string "Hostname"
    default "cube"
    help
        DHCP and mDNS name: the cube answers at http://<hostname>.local/.

config CUBE_OTA_TOKEN
    string "Update token"
    default ""
    help
        If set, an update must carry the header
        "Authorization: Bearer <token>". Empty lets anyone on the network
        update the cube.

endmenu

endmenu
